  "body": "### What are you trying to do\n\n<img width=\"1942\" height=\"853\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1fbff08f-9eba-44d1-b5ee-58efdf43ea3e\" />\n\nThe text in the trace window should be highlightable and copyable with right click Copy.\n\nCode tracing appears to be enabled by default.\n\nThe line that is being traced should be highlighted so that the user can see which one it is.\n\nThe user should be able to click on a line and the trace updates to show where it is.\n\nIf the trace checkbox is clicked the GCode window goes full width and blocks the part.\n\n<img width=\"1948\" height=\"906\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e0c129fd-b702-4c29-a1a6-03c72aae00bc\" />\n\nNot my project but I'd set this to high priority even though it is a Feature because testers need this to work to go through the GCode with a find tooth comb to make sure it is doing what it is supposed to prior to running it.\n\n\n\n\n### How you imagine it working\n\n_No response_",
